# Cursor collapse diagnostic — 2026-06-06 ~22:27–22:39
# Log sources: ~/Library/Application Support/Cursor/logs/20260606T124705/

## Symptom
Agent chat refreshes / collapses mid-run; verification never completes; session state lost.

## Root cause (confirmed, repeated 8+ times tonight)

Browser MCP hydration-check workflow triggers extension-host restart:

1. Agent calls browser MCP: navigate → lock → CDP Emulation → Log.enable → Runtime.enable → Page.reload
2. Renderer floods console via WebviewBrowserManager; retention cap engages
3. Main UI thread blocks ~15s (RendererPing threshold)
4. Extension hosts exit; Browser Automation MCP Provider disposed
5. In-flight browser_cdp calls canceled; agent IPC disconnects
6. Cursor window reloads extension host; chat/agent state lost

## Key log lines (verbatim)

### main.log
[RendererPing] enabled (intervalMs=5000, blockThresholdMs=15000, stacks=true)
[RendererPing] window 7 (pid 89938) blocked for ~15003ms
Extension host with pid 85113 exited with code: 0
[PowerMainService] Releasing 1 orphaned wakelock(s) for owner=window:7 releaseReason=ipc-client-disconnect

### renderer.log (repeats on every attempt)
[WebviewBrowserManager] Console-log retention cap engaged; older or duplicate entries will be elided.
OpenInBrowserWatcher: Detected URL to open - Pattern: nextjs, URL: http://localhost:3000

### Cursor IDE Browser Automation.log (typical crash sequence)
Executing tool: browser_cdp ... Log.enable
Executing tool: browser_cdp ... Runtime.enable
Executing tool: browser_cdp ... Page.reload ... ignoreCache:true
Browser Automation MCP Provider disposed
Error executing tool browser_cdp:: Canceled

## Contributing factors
- CDP Log.enable + Runtime.enable + injected console capture = high log volume
- Multiple navigates/reloads per hydration check
- npm run dev stdout triggers OpenInBrowserWatcher (extra browser activity)
- Long shell Await (45s+) on dev-server startup also interrupted prior runs

## Safer alternatives for verification
- Run Playwright/puppeteer script in terminal (no Browser MCP)
- Manual check in browser DevTools
- Split agent steps: start dev server first, verify in separate message
- Avoid Log.enable/Runtime.enable; use Runtime.evaluate once after load
